<title>GREECE: BARINGS SETS $CALL WARRANTS ON GREEK BANK BASKET.</title>
<headline>BARINGS SETS $CALL WARRANTS ON GREEK BANK BASKET.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following information on</p>
<p>100,000 American style $call warrants on a basket of six Greek</p>
<p>banking shares launched by ING Baring Financial Products today</p>
<p>was provided by the Greek placing agent Sigma Securities.</p>
<p>ISSUER:			 IBFP</p>
<p>GREEK PLACEMENT AGENT:    Sigma Securities</p>
<p>WARRANT STYLE &amp;TYPE:	American style, $composite call, cash</p>
<p>				  settlement</p>
<p>ISSUE PRICE:		  $12.50 per warrant (also payable in</p>
<p>				  Greek drachmas)</p>
<p>LAUNCH DATE:		  October 8th, 1996</p>
<p>EXPIRATION DATE:		     12 months after the issue date</p>
<p>ISSUE DATE-PREMIUM PAYMENT DAY:  Launch date plus 21 business</p>
<p>					   days</p>
<p>REFERENCE BASKET:		    Stocks	  Initial weighting</p>
<p>				    Alpha Credit Bank     25.0%</p>
<p>				    ErgoBank		  20.0%</p>
<p>				    National Bank/Greece  25.0%</p>
<p>				    Commercial Bank/Greece 15.0%</p>
<p>				    National Mortgage Bank 7.5%</p>
<p>				    Ionian Bank		7.5%</p>
<p>LISTING:			  Application will be made to list the</p>
<p>				    warrants on the Luxemburg Stock</p>
<p>				    Exchange. Listing expected but not</p>
<p>				    guaranteed to be granted within</p>
<p>				    three weeks from the issue date.</p>
<p>GOVERNING LAW:		  English</p>
<p>SELLING RESTRICTIONS:	 U.K.</p>
<p>MINIMUM TRADING SIZE:	 100 warrants in denominations of one</p>
<p>				    warrant</p>
<p>GEARING:			  8.0X</p>
<p>COMMON DEPOSITORY:	    Chase Manhattan Bank</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
